      "writtenOn": "2025-11-12T15:15:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "A deadlock can happen here if an other core is in the middle of handling a `CPU_SUSPEND/CPU_OFF`. These calls first lock the `CpuPowerNode`, then its ancestor `NonCpuPowerNode`, while this locking happens in the opposite order here.\nThis function should lock all `CpuPowerNodes` in one sequence without locking `NonCpuPowerNodes`.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 361,
        "startChar": 47,
        "endLine": 361,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "bbefc08af6191618c96601908b6215dc2633f9a3",
